    },
    turnFlow: 'Deal: 6 cards to talon, then 12 to each player in two rounds of 6; anticlockwise. Optional throw-in if dealt no taroks; optional declaration of four kings before bidding. Bidding: Forant (right of dealer) starts; each player once may bid 1–4 (talon cards to take) or pass; 4 only after a 3. Declarer calls a king by suit; its holder is partner (secret). Optional king ultimo, kontra. Talon exchange: declarer takes 0–3 cards per bid, discards same number; may not discard 5-point cards or taroks unless unavoidable. Announcements: trul, last-trick-with-lowest-trump, taroki count, etc., in anticlockwise order from declarer. Play: Forant leads; must follow suit or play a tarok; if no suit and no tarok, any card (cannot win). Trick to highest tarok, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next.',
