      'Setup example: 12 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Declarer's team wins by capturing more than half the card points (at least 35 of 70) in tricks plus their share of the talon. Opponents win if they have 35 or more. Game and bonuses (trul, last-trick-with-lowest-trump, kings, etc.) are scored and paid independently.",
      'Turn-flow example: Deal: 6 cards to talon, then 12 to each player in two rounds of 6; anticlockwise. Optional throw-in if dealt no taroks; optional declaration of four kings before bidding. Bidding: Forant (right of dealer) starts; each player once may bid 1–4 (talon cards to take) or pass; 4 only after a 3. Declarer calls a king by suit; its holder is partner (secret). Optional king ultimo, kontra. Talon exchange: declarer takes 0–3 cards per bid, discards same number; may not discard 5-point cards or taroks unless unavoidable. Announcements: trul, last-trick-with-lowest-trump, taroki count, etc., in anticlockwise order from declarer. Play: Forant leads; must follow suit or play a tarok; if no suit and no tarok, any card (cannot win). Trick to highest tarok, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next.',
